This repo has a local Graphify knowledge graph at `graphify-out/`. Always query it before exploring source with Grep, Glob, Read, or shell search.

Run Graphify from the project root (`/Users/pavelpugacev/Downloads/Tower ganme`). Do not grep `node_modules/`. Do not paste `graph.json` into prompts.

**Required before codebase exploration (you and every subagent):**

```
graphify query "<question>"
graphify path "<FromSymbol>" "<ToSymbol>"
graphify explain "<symbol or concept>"
```

Useful extras:

```
graphify query "<question>" --budget 4000
graphify affected "<symbol>"
graphify god-nodes --top 15
```

Put this block in every subagent prompt that explores or explains code:

```
Before Grep/Read/Glob, run from the project root:
graphify query "<question>"
graphify path "<A>" "<B>"
graphify explain "<symbol>"
Then open only the files the graph names.
```

Use Read/Grep/Glob only after Graphify has named the files and symbols, or if `graphify-out/graph.json` is missing.

After you change code, refresh the graph (AST-only, no API key):

```
npm run graphify:update
```

or `graphify update .`. Full rebuild without LLM: `graphify extract . --code-only`. Then `graphify cluster-only . --no-label` if `GRAPH_REPORT.md` is stale.

Read `graphify-out/GRAPH_REPORT.md` only for a broad architecture pass when query/path/explain are not enough. Open `graphify-out/graph.html` in a browser to inspect the graph. Never commit `graphify-out/`.
